    <string name="support_faq_intro">Up-to-date answers to common questions. If you can\'t find a solution, message us.</string>
    <string name="support_contact_button">Message support</string>
    <string name="faq_q_connect">How do I connect to the VPN?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_connect">On the home screen, select Automatic or a specific server, then tap the large round button. The first time you connect, approve Android\'s system request to create a VPN connection.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_connecting_check">Why doesn\'t “Connecting…” immediately change to “Connected”?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_connecting_check">Starting the VPN core is not enough: ToBeVPN first sends a test request through the selected server. “Connected” appears only after real traffic is confirmed. If the check fails, the app attempts to recover the tunnel and then shows an error instead of giving a false impression that the VPN works.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_slow">The VPN won\'t connect or is slow</string>
    <string name="faq_a_slow">Make sure your regular internet connection works and turn off any other VPN app. If the selected server fails the traffic check, refresh the server list with the button in the top-right corner, choose another available server, and reconnect. You can check tunnel speed with the built-in speed test after connecting.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_server">How do I choose the right server?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_server">Automatic considers availability, current TCP ping, and the history of successful and failed connections. A more reliable server may therefore be selected instead of the one with the lowest ping. With manual selection, a lower ping usually means lower latency, but it does not guarantee the highest speed.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_stats">Where can I view traffic usage and statistics?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_stats">The Current session card on the home screen shows traffic and time for the active connection. Tap it to see daily, weekly, and monthly statistics stored on this device. The quota in the Subscription card is loaded from the server for your account and plan, so it is not the same value as local session statistics.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_quick_settings">Can I connect from Android Quick Settings?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_quick_settings">Yes. Edit the Android Quick Settings panel and add the ToBeVPN tile. The first use may open the app to request Android\'s VPN permission. After that, the tile connects the selected or automatically chosen server and disconnects the VPN with one tap.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_pay">How do I pay for, renew or change a subscription?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_pay">Open the Subscription card on the home screen, choose a plan and duration, tap Buy, and complete payment in Telegram. Available payment methods and the final price are loaded from the server for your account.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_activate">My subscription did not update after payment</string>
    <string name="faq_a_activate">Return to ToBeVPN and wait a few minutes: the app checks the payment automatically. Make sure you are using the same Telegram account. If the status does not change, restart the app and contact support with the approximate payment time.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_discount">Where do I apply a promo code and see the discount?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_discount">Open Settings → Promo codes, enter the code, and tap Apply. Subscription days, traffic, devices, or another reward are added automatically. An active discount appears in a separate card and is already included in the final Subscription price. The list below is application history: a one-time discount shown there may already have been used.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_devices">How do I connect a phone, computer, or Android TV?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_devices">On the new device, choose sign-in through another device to get a QR code or connection code. On a phone already signed in, open Advanced → Devices, scan the QR code or enter the code, and confirm. If you reached your plan\'s device limit, disconnect an unused device first.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_app_filter">Can I enable the VPN only for selected apps?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_app_filter">Yes. Open Advanced → VPN apps and choose a mode: all apps, selected apps only, or all except selected apps. The VPN reconnects to apply the change.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_referrals">How do invitations and rewards work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_referrals">Share your personal link from Referrals. Extra days are added automatically after an invited user buys or renews a subscription. Current terms are available from the information button next to the invited-friends count. An inviter\'s Telegram ID can be set only once.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_updates">How do I update the app?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_updates">Open About and tap Check. The Google Play build updates through Google Play, while a build installed from an APK offers to download and install updates inside ToBeVPN.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_display_scale">What if the interface or text is too small?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_display_scale">Open Personalization → Display size and text. You can adjust the interface and font sizes independently, enable bold or outlined text, preview the result, and reset the settings.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_diagnostics">How do I record and share a diagnostic log?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_diagnostics">Open About and hold the ToBeVPN logo for one second. After diagnostic mode is enabled, the Diagnostics card appears: tap Start collection, reproduce the issue, then open Log history and share the required day. Logs stay only on the device: up to 10 MB per day and no more than the latest 7 days. They are never sent automatically. Holding the logo again disables the mode and stops collection.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_privacy">What data does the app store?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_privacy">The VPN encrypts the connection between your device and the VPN server. We do not store a list of visited sites or traffic contents. Technical diagnostics are off by default: logs started manually stay locally for up to 7 days and are never sent without your action.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_support_details">What should I include when contacting support?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_support_details">Describe the issue and the steps before it, and include your device model, Android version, ToBeVPN version, selected server, and approximate failure time. If a technical log is needed, support will explain how to enable diagnostics and export the required day.</string>
